# Code owners
#
# Every path here is somewhere a subtle mistake is expensive and hard to see.
# Listing them requests review automatically, so these changes cannot be merged
# without at least being put in front of someone.
#
# NOTE: with required approvals currently set to 0 (single-maintainer repository
# — see docs/operations/branch-protection.md), CODEOWNERS requests review but
# does not block merge. Turning approvals on makes it binding, and nothing else
# has to change.

# Default
*                                                           @YonatanVol

# Availability resolution — the logic that decides whether a product can be
# sold and what delivery it promises. Wrong here means overselling.
/wp-content/plugins/electricchic-core/includes/Availability/ @YonatanVol

# Pricing and margin. Wrong here means selling below cost, silently.
/wp-content/plugins/electricchic-core/includes/Pricing/      @YonatanVol

# Payment, invoicing and webhook handling. Wrong here means money or tax
# documents going astray, usually without an error being raised.
/wp-content/plugins/electricchic-core/includes/Integrations/ @YonatanVol

# Returns and refunds — customer money and stock accuracy.
/wp-content/plugins/electricchic-core/includes/Returns/      @YonatanVol

# CI, deployment and the rules that enforce everything else.
/.github/workflows/                                          @YonatanVol
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                          @YonatanVol

# The sniff that mechanically enforces HPOS compliance.
/tools/phpcs/                                                @YonatanVol
